+---
+id: task-001-add-rental-module-createrentalservice
+type: task
+title: "Add rental module createRentalService"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Export `createRentalService()` from `src/index.ts`: an in-memory rental service for the booking desk,
+covering equipment catalogue, quoting and booking, per the school's rules (integer cents, UTC ISO-8601
+whole-day periods, no double-booking). Cancellation is explicitly out of scope for this request.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Added `src/index.ts` exporting `createRentalService()`, returning `{ addEquipment, quote, book }`
+  backed by in-memory `Map`/array state (equipment catalogue, booked periods per item, booking list).
+- `addEquipment(item)` validates `kind` is `'board' | 'sail'` and `dailyPrice` is a non-negative integer
+  (cents), per rule 1.
+- A shared `parsePeriod`/`resolveQuote` path validates: the item exists, both `start` and `end` parse as
+  ISO-8601 timestamps, both fall exactly at UTC midnight (`ms % DAY_MS === 0`, true for any UTC midnight
+  under Unix time), and `end` is strictly after `start` — enforcing whole-day-only periods (rule 3).
+- `quote(request)` returns `{ itemId, start, end, total }` with `total = days * dailyPrice`.
+- `book(request)` re-runs the same validation, additionally checks the new period against the item's
+  already-booked periods for overlap (half-open interval comparison, so back-to-back bookings are
+  allowed), then records the period and returns a `Booking` with a deterministic incrementing id
+  (`booking-<n>`, no randomness/wall-clock per the determinism directive).
+- Did not implement cancellation, as instructed; the cancellation policy (rule 5) is documented in the
+  decision log for future work.
+- Added `src/index.test.ts` (red-first: written and run before the implementation existed, confirmed
+  failing, then made green) covering: happy-path quoting and booking, unknown item for both `quote` and
+  `book`, non-midnight period, non-advancing period, overlapping bookings, back-to-back non-overlapping
+  bookings, unknown equipment kind, and invalid `dailyPrice`.
+- Verified with `npm test` (Node's built-in `node --test`, which natively type-strips `.ts` files on
+  Node 22.23 — no build step or extra dependency needed): all 10 tests pass.
+- Confirmed `src/index.ts` itself type-checks cleanly under the project's `strict` `tsconfig.json` (using
+  a scratch TypeScript install, not added to the repo). The only `tsc` errors are pre-existing project
+  setup gaps in `src/index.test.ts` (no `@types/node`, and `tsconfig.json` lacks
+  `allowImportingTsExtensions` for the `.ts`-suffixed relative import) that predate this change and are
+  unrelated to runtime correctness; left untouched since adding dependencies/tooling wasn't requested.
